 "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42535808"}, {"study_label": "Idebenone SR (meta)", "outcome": "visual improvement in both eyes after unilateral injection", "arm": "standard", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42535808"}, {"study_label": "rAAV2/2-ND4 (meta)", "outcome": "best-corrected visual acuity", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42131170"}, {"study_label": "rAAV2/2-ND4 (meta)", "outcome": "responder rates", "arm": "mito", "direction": "neutral", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42131170"}, {"study_label": "rAAV2/2-ND4 (meta)", "outcome": "adverse events (safety profile)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42131170"}, {"study_label": "NFS-02 (Ph2)", "outcome": "safety/tolerability", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT05820152"}, {"study_label": "NFS-02 (Ph2)", "outcome": "visual acuity", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT05820152"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "elamipretide", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 5, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42794697", "40816230", "NCT05168774", "NCT07531251", "NCT05162768"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 3, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42361626", "42229401", "42032617"]}, {"intervention": "nicotinamide riboside", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42669151"]}, {"intervention": "mesenchymal stem cells (mitochondrial transfer)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42453608"]}, {"intervention": "MNV-201 (placenta-derived mitochondrial cell therapy)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT06017869"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42324025", "42495453"]}, {"intervention": "elamipretide", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42290373"]}, {"intervention": "nicotinamide riboside", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 3, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT05732051", "NCT07563322", "NCT04913805"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42616901"]}, {"intervention": "mitochondria-targeted nanotherapy", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42022751"]}, {"intervention": "mitophagy modulation", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42746169"]}, {"intervention": "ND4 gene therapy (rAAV)", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42627399", "42131170"]}, {"intervention": "idebenone (standard of care)", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42608929", "42535808"]}, {"intervention": "NFS-02 (mitochondrial-augmentation cell therapy)", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT05820152"]}, {"intervention": "supportive care (standard of care)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 0, "top_evidence": null, "refs": []}, {"intervention": "guideline-directed medical therapy (standard of care)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 0, "top_evidence": null, "refs": []}], "insights": ["Elamipretide is the only approved mitochondria-targeted therapy, and its accelerated approval rests on muscle-strength improvement alone; cardiac disease modification remains unconfirmed, and its Phase 3 (NCT05162768) and Phase 4 (NCT07531251) RCTs have no posted results, so no head-to-head benefit over supportive care is established; a single n=1 case report suggests sustained clinical benefit (42794697, NCT05162768, NCT07531251, 40816230).", "No standard-of-care arm data exist in this corpus for either supportive care in primary mitochondrial diseases or GDMT in heart failure; the comparison is therefore mito-arm-only for those diseases, and this is reported as a genuine evidence gap rather than an invented standard side (42361626).", "Chronic heart failure: no record reports a statistically significant clinical benefit for any mitochondria-targeted agent; all three clinical trials (NR Ph1 crossover pilot n=10; PLC+NR Ph2 n=53; NR Ph2 n=60) have no posted results, and the only significant positive effects are preclinical (elamipretide muscle force +8.2 to +173%, P<=0.041; in silico reperfusion model; urolithin A signals are positive but non-significant) (42290373, 42625359, 42616901, NCT07563322, NCT04913805, NCT05732051).", "LHON: gene therapy is the most promising experimental direction - the rAAV2/2-ND4 meta-analysis shows significantly improved BCVA (though responder rates did not significantly increase) - while the standard of care, idebenone, is itself weakly supported, with one meta-analysis rating effectiveness unclear and a systematic review reporting significant partial visual recovery with early treatment; the two idebenone metas thus disagree and the uncertainty is carried into the standard-side markers (42131170, 42627399, 42608929, 42535808).", "Honest negative/safety signals: preclinical nicotinamide riboside aggravated anemia in a bone-marrow model (impaired heme biosynthesis and erythrocyte maturation) despite positive cardiac contractility, and the LHON gene-therapy meta-analysis noted adverse events in some studies (mostly mild ocular inflammation, no treatment-related mortality); IV NAD+ administration additionally lacks robust clinical validation (42669151, 42627399, 42131170, 42489969).", "MitoQ, the most studied mitochondria-targeted antioxidant, has only review/meta-level and preclinical evidence across primary mitochondrial diseases, heart failure, and Alzheimer's disease, with no significant clinical effect in any record; haplogroup-dependent penetrance in m.11778G>A LHON should inform trial stratification (42361626, 42229401, 42032617, 42324025, 42495453, 41596136, 42632451)."]}